# Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres (Prisma)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two URLs, because they are used by different things:
#
#   DATABASE_URL  Supavisor transaction pooler, port 6543. Used at runtime by
#                 src/lib/prisma.ts. Serverless instances are ephemeral and
#                 scale out fast, so the app must never open direct backend
#                 connections -- it would exhaust the instance's connection
#                 limit under a traffic spike. `pgbouncer=true` is required.
#
#   DIRECT_URL    Direct/session connection, port 5432. Used by prisma migrate
#                 (see prisma.config.ts) and by nothing else.
#
# The `prisma` role is a dedicated database user -- create it in the Supabase
# SQL editor rather than reusing the postgres superuser. Note that it is a
# privileged role that is NOT constrained by RLS; see prisma/migrations/
# ..._add_ownership_and_rls for why that is intentional and what still
# enforces authorization.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://prisma.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"
DIRECT_URL="postgres://prisma.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# Local development with `supabase start` instead:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Auth
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both are publishable. The anon key is designed to ship to the browser and is
# what the Data API sees; RLS is what protects the rows behind it.
#
# Next inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* at BUILD time, so these must also be present at
# build time, not only at runtime.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://PROJECT_REF.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-publishable-key"

# NEVER set the service-role key in this app. It bypasses RLS completely, and
# anything in apps/mtg can end up in a client bundle. The crawler is the only
# component that has a reason to hold it.
